# SERVER OWNERSHIP & BUSINESS INTELLIGENCE DASHBOARD
## Full Application Development Specification

# 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW

Build a modern, lightweight web application designed to provide centralised visibility of server infrastructure, ownership, business units, technical relationships and operational responsibilities.

The application will ingest server inventory data from CSV files or a database and transform it into an interactive dashboard.

The primary purpose is to support Security Operations, Infrastructure Operations, Vulnerability Management and Incident Response teams.

The application must make it easy to:

- Identify server owners and their contact details.
- Identify the business unit responsible for a server.
- Understand relationships between servers, business units, support teams and infrastructure.
- Investigate incidents and determine potential business impact.
- Identify servers requiring patching or remediation.
- Generate affected-server lists for vulnerability assessments.
- Quickly identify the correct contacts for incident communications.
- Visualise infrastructure relationships through interactive diagrams.
- Search and filter infrastructure records using multiple attributes.
- Generate communication-ready reports.

This is an operational intelligence platform, not simply an asset inventory application.

The interface should feel like a modern SOC platform: clean, professional, dark, lightweight, responsive and information-dense without becoming cluttered.

