## 3.1 Database technology

Use PostgreSQL as the preferred production database.

For a local prototype, SQLite is acceptable if the application uses a database abstraction layer that makes migration to PostgreSQL straightforward.

Do not use browser localStorage as the primary database.

The application must be capable of handling tens of thousands of server records without significant performance degradation.

