# 10. OWNERSHIP EXPLORER

Build an interactive ownership visualisation.

This should help users understand the relationship between organisational structures and server infrastructure.

Use a graph visualisation library such as React Flow, Cytoscape.js or D3.

Preferred option: Cytoscape.js for larger relationship graphs.

## 10.1 Graph structure

The graph should represent:

Business Unit
    |
    +-- Sub-Business Unit
            |
            +-- Product
                    |
                    +-- Function
                            |
                            +-- Server
                                    |
                                    +-- Hypervisor Host
                                    |
                                    +-- Datacenter
                                    |
                                    +-- Network
                                    |
                                    +-- Manager
                                    |
                                    +-- Support Team

This is a conceptual relationship model, not a mandatory ownership hierarchy.

Do not imply that every relationship is a parent-child relationship.

For example, managers and support teams should be represented as associated entities rather than incorrectly placed in the organisational hierarchy.

## 10.2 Graph interactions

Users should be able to:

- Click nodes.
- Expand related nodes.
- Collapse branches.
- Drag nodes.
- Zoom in and out.
- Search nodes.
- Highlight relationships.
- Filter node types.
- Reset the graph.
- Export the graph as an image.

When selecting a node, display an information panel.

Example:

Selecting "John Lennon" should display:

- Email address.
- Associated business units.
- Number of managed servers.
- Server hostnames.
- Datacenters.
- Networks.

Selecting "BRICK" should display:

- Organisation information.
- Associated business units.
- Server count.
- Managers.
- Products.
- Infrastructure.

Selecting a server should open the Server Detail page.

## 10.3 Graph performance

Do not render every server and relationship simultaneously.

Implement progressive expansion.

Start with business units.

Expand into sub-business units.

Expand into products.

Expand into servers.

Load relationships when requested.

Provide graph filtering and search before rendering large datasets.

